          "code": "CSR_SKILL_TOPICS_EXTRACTIONS",
          "id": "1766075916136",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766075916139_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Context\nA user can post a question containing skills and expects people who are experts in those topics to answer the question.\nWe need to identify potential skills from the question.\n\n##Instruction\nGiven a question {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.questiontext}}, identify the skills from the question.\n\nDefinition of Skills\nSkills are abilities or areas of expertise a person can develop, demonstrate, or be trained in.\n\nExamples: leadership, teamwork, critical thinking, design thinking, marketing, project management, programming, adaptability, machine learning, negotiation techniques.\nExclude job titles, project or business outcomes, objectives, roles, job contexts, timeframes, or other non-ability phrases.\n\n##Acceptance Criteria\nExtraction Rules:\nExtract only skills as contiguous words or noun phrases (maximum four words) directly from the question.\nThe extracted phrase should be an ability, area of expertise, or learnable method—not a job title, role, outcome, objective, group, or general business area.\nDo not extract job titles, project roles, teams, locations, business functions, context, or timeframes.\nDo not fragment multi-word skills; if the skill is a multi-word phrase, only extract the full phrase as it appears.\nDo not rephrase, infer, or use synonyms.\nDo not extract or split context, outcomes, or beneficiary/object phrases (e.g., “user experience”, “team performance”, “investment decisions”, “product launches”, “cloud deployments”).\nDo not extract adjectives, verbs, or adverbs.\nExamples\nPositive Examples\nQ: Is project management software necessary for large projects?\nExtract: \"project management\"\nQ: Should emotional intelligence be part of employee training?\nExtract: \"emotional intelligence\"\nQ: Does supply chain optimization improve efficiency?\nExtract: \"supply chain optimization\"\nQ: Is machine learning valuable in data science roles?\nExtract: \"machine learning\"\nNegative Examples\nQ: Can workflow optimization increase productivity?\nExtract: \"workflow optimization\" (do NOT extract \"productivity\")\nQ: Should spreadsheet modeling be taught to interns?\nExtract: \"spreadsheet modeling\" (do NOT extract \"interns\")\nQ: Does creative thinking boost problem identification?\nExtract: \"creative thinking\" (do NOT extract \"problem identification\")\nQ: Is strategic planning the foundation of business growth?\nExtract: \"strategic planning\" (do NOT extract \"business growth\")\nQ: Why is leadership crucial for organizational culture?\nExtract: \"leadership\" (do NOT extract \"organizational culture\")\nQ: Are negotiation techniques essential for sales success?\nExtract: \"negotiation techniques\" (do NOT extract \"sales success\")\nQ: Should agile methodology be mandated for IT projects?\nExtract: \"agile methodology\" (do NOT extract \"IT projects\")\nQ: What is the impact of communication on project timelines?\nExtract: \"communication\" (do NOT extract \"project timelines\")\nQ: When is requirements documentation key to software projects?\nExtract: \"requirements documentation\" (do NOT extract \"software projects\")\nQ: Does peer mentoring accelerate onboarding?\nExtract: \"peer mentoring\" (do NOT extract \"onboarding\")\n\n##Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in this format:\n{\n\"results\": {\n\"skills\": [\n{ \"skill\": \"\" }\n]\n}\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
